# Line endings that survive a Windows clone.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which writes every text file
# with CRLF. Shell scripts copied into images and executed there fail with
# `exec /app/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory` — a message about a
# file that exists. Pin LF for everything a container or make consumes.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# Two branches that each add an entry at the top of the same CHANGELOG section
# stop a merge with a conflict whose resolution is always "keep both lines" —
# a quarter of the returns from review in one measured week. The built-in union
# driver keeps both sides' lines instead. It can put the two entries in either
# order and never drops a duplicate, so the merged section is still read.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
